In .NET 10 (starting with .NET 9 SR10+), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated on Android because the underlying `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` flag was removed by Google.

The recommended replacement is to use **edge-to-edge display with keyboard insets**. Here's what to do:

### 1. Enable edge-to-edge + keyboard handling in your `MainActivity`

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Enable edge-to-edge rendering
    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

    // Listen for keyboard (IME) insets and adjust padding
    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBars = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Use the larger of IME or system bar bottom inset
        int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBars.Bottom);
        v.SetPadding(systemBars.Left, systemBars.Top, systemBars.Right, bottom);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

### 2. Remove the old platform-specific code

Delete any usage of:
```csharp
// No longer works — remove this
App.Current.On<Android>()
    .UseWindowSoftInputModeAdjust(WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize);
```

### 3. (Optional) Animate the transition

Add `WindowCompat.GetInsetsController(Window!, Window!.DecorView).ControlWindowInsetsAnimation(...)` or use `WindowInsetsAnimationCompat` if you want a smooth slide-up animation matching the keyboard.

---

**Why this works:** Android 11+ uses the `WindowInsets` API for keyboard visibility. The `Ime()` inset type reports the keyboard height, and adjusting padding on the decor view pushes your content (including the bottom input bar) above the keyboard.
